# The SAME calc.fdf used for structure.fdf's own real relaxation (same
# basis/k-points/XC/SCF) -- stb-elasticInputs never regenerates any of
# this, it only writes the strained structure and adds one %include line
# (see the README, section 2). This is the file you pass as --calc.
#
# Deliberately kept WITH its real MD.TypeOfRun/MD.VariableCell/MD.Steps
# block still active (exactly as it came from the real relaxation this
# structure went through) -- unlike stb-strain, stb-elasticInputs does not
# need a "correct" relaxation block here to work right: every generated
# folder is FORCED to a pure single-point SCF regardless of what this
# block says, via a %include prepended at the very top of the copy it
# writes. The README's "gotcha, live" (section 2.2) proves this override
# actually wins over the MD.Steps 200/MD.VariableCell true below.

## ===================================================================
## SYSTEM DEFINITION
## ===================================================================
SystemLabel      siesta
SystemName       siesta

## Include the structure file generated with STB-SUITE
%include structure.fdf

## ===================================================================
## BASIS SET DEFINITION
## ===================================================================
PAO.BasisType       split
PAO.BasisSize       DZP
PAO.EnergyShift     0.01 Ry

## ===================================================================
## K-POINT SAMPLING (BRILLOUIN ZONE)
## ===================================================================
kgrid.MonkhorstPack   [12  12  1]
Mesh.CutOff           320  Ry
FilterCutoff          150  Ry

## ===================================================================
## EXCHANGE-CORRELATION (XC) FUNCTIONAL
## ===================================================================
XC.Functional       GGA
XC.Authors          PBE

## ===================================================================
## SPIN POLARIZATION
## ===================================================================
Spin                non-polarized

## ===================================================================
## SELF-CONSISTENT-FIELD (SCF)
## ===================================================================
MaxSCFIterations        300
SCF.Mixer.Weight        0.1
SCF.DM.Tolerance        1.0d-5  eV
SCF.Mixer.History       6
ElectronicTemperature   300 K
Diag.ParallelOverK      .true.

## ===================================================================
## VAN DER WAALS CORRECTIONS (GRIMME DFT-D3)
## ===================================================================
# A 2D monolayer's own interlayer/vdW interactions don't apply here (no
# second layer), but DFT-D3 also corrects intra-layer dispersion -- kept
# on since that's what the real reference relaxation used.
DFTD3                   .true.

## ===================================================================
## STRUCTURE RELAXATION (MOLECULAR DYNAMICS - MD)
## ===================================================================
## Real, active relaxation settings -- deliberately NOT single-point.
## stb-elasticInputs forces every generated folder to single-point
## regardless (see the header comment above and the README's section 2).
MD.TypeOfRun            CG
MD.VariableCell         true
MD.MaxForceTol          0.01 eV/Ang
MD.Steps                200

## ===================================================================
## STARTING THE CALCULATION (Using previous results)
## ===================================================================
DM.UseSaveDM            .true.

## ===================================================================
## OUTPUT FILES
## ===================================================================
WriteCoorInitial        .true.
WriteForces             .true.
